Character death sucks... it's a given.  But Nethack is fun in that
while character death is pretty bad, it's not ALL bad.  Lately I've
been given to the same thought whenever a really promising character
dies: "Ohh, drat.  Oh well, their bones pile will be awesome."

(Note that I don't play with Hearse, my only Nethack engine being an
ancient laptop with no modem)

My deepest bones pile was a monk who was killed by a minotaur in the
mazes before the Castle.  I was really, really irked at myself, because
I'd let myself get cocky about her and forgotten that minotaurs hurt a
lot.  But there's a big difference between a monk with AC -10 and a
ranger with Stormbringer and AC -20.  And when I found out which level
I'd just gotten this ranger to...

The feeling you get when you have a character who's doing really well,
and then you get to level 20 or so and find the bones pile of a
character that was doing really well... that's awesome.

---What's the best bones pile you've ever run into?---  Doesn't have to
be one of your characters necessarily, it could be through Hearse.

For the record, my ranger already was ready to storm the castle, and
the monk corpse had a magic lamp, speed boots, gauntlets of power, and
a bag of holding containing mass amounts of sheer useful Stuff.


